```cpp
#include <hexi/hexi.h>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <cstdint>

struct NetworkPacket {
    uint32_t packet_id;
    std::string username;
    std::vector<uint32_t> scores;
    std::string metadata;

    void serialise(auto& stream) {
        // Write packet_id directly
        stream << packet_id;

        // Write username with length prefix (default behavior for strings)
        stream << username;

        // Write scores count first, then the vector elements
        uint32_t scores_count = static_cast<uint32_t>(scores.size());
        stream << scores_count;
        stream << scores;

        // Write null-terminated metadata
        stream << hexi::null_terminated(metadata);
    }
};

std::vector<uint8_t> serialize_packet(const NetworkPacket& packet) {
    // Create a buffer to hold the serialized data
    std::vector<uint8_t> buffer;

    // Create a buffer adaptor
    hexi::buffer_adaptor adaptor(buffer);

    // Create a binary stream
    hexi::binary_stream stream(adaptor);

    // Serialize the packet using the stream's serialise method
    stream.serialise(packet);

    // Return the populated buffer
    return buffer;
}
```

**Explanation:**

1. **`serialise` method in `NetworkPacket`**:
   - `stream << packet_id`: Writes the packet ID as a uint32_t
   - `stream << username`: Writes the username string with a length prefix (default behavior for std::string in Hexi)
   - `stream << scores_count; stream << scores;`: First writes the count of scores, then writes the vector using operator<< which internally calls write_container
   - `stream << hexi::null_terminated(metadata)`: Writes the metadata string with a null terminator using the `null_terminated` adaptor

2. **`serialize_packet` function**:
   - Creates a `std::vector<uint8_t>` buffer to store the serialized data
   - Creates a `hexi::buffer_adaptor` wrapping the buffer
   - Creates a `hexi::binary_stream` using the adaptor
   - Calls `stream.serialise(packet)` which invokes the `NetworkPacket::serialise` method
   - Returns the buffer containing the serialized data

