1. Create a binary stream with a buffer adaptor
2. Use the `deserialise` method to deserialize the object

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/hexi.h>
#include <string>
#include <cstdint>
#include <span>

struct UserData {
    uint64_t user_id;
    uint8_t age;
    std::string name;

    void serialise(auto& stream) {
        stream(user_id, age, name);
    }
};

UserData deserialize_user_data(const std::span<const uint8_t> buffer) {
    // Create a buffer adaptor with the input buffer
    hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor adaptor(const_cast<std::span<const uint8_t>&>(buffer));

    // Create a binary stream using the adaptor
    hexi::pmc::binary_stream stream(adaptor);

    // Create a UserData object to deserialize into
    UserData user_data{};

    // Deserialize the object
    stream.deserialise(user_data);

    return user_data;
}
```

Note: The `buffer_adaptor` in the PMC (Polymorphic) namespace works with non-const references, so I needed to cast away the const. If this is an issue, an alternative approach would be to copy the buffer data first:

```cpp
