- `enter_thread_with_allocator`: Calls `enter_thread()` on the allocator to initialize the thread-local storage for the current thread
- `exit_thread_with_allocator`: Calls `exit_thread()` on the allocator to clean up the thread-local storage and release any resources allocated for the current thread

These methods ensure proper lifecycle management of the TLS allocator, allowing it to track which thread is using it and manage thread-specific allocation state correctly.

