bool check_can_write_seek(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer) {
    // Check if the buffer supports write seeking
    return buffer.can_write_seek();
}

void seek_write_position(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer, hexi::buffer_seek direction, std::size_t offset) {
    // Seek the write position using write_seek() with different seek directions
    buffer.write_seek(direction, offset);
}

void update_header_at_position(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer, uint32_t header_value) {
    // Save current position by writing a placeholder header first
    // Write placeholder header (4 bytes for uint32_t)
    std::uint32_t placeholder = 0;
    buffer.write(placeholder);

    // Save the position after the header (which is the current write position)
    // Now write some body data (example)
    std::uint32_t body_data = 0x12345678;
    buffer.write(body_data);

    // Seek back to the beginning to update the header
    // Use buffer_seek::beg (absolute position) to go to position 0
    buffer.write_seek(hexi::buffer_seek::beg, 0);

    // Write the actual header value
    buffer.write(header_value);

    // Seek to the end to continue writing if needed
    buffer.write_seek(hexi::buffer_seek::end, 0);
}
```

**Explanation:**

1. **`check_can_write_seek`**: Simply calls the `can_write_seek()` method on the buffer adaptor, which returns a boolean indicating whether write seeking is supported.

2. **`seek_write_position`**: Calls the `write_seek()` method with the specified direction and offset. The `buffer_seek` enum can have values like:
   - `hexi::buffer_seek::beg` - seek from beginning (absolute position)
   - `hexi::buffer_seek::cur` - seek from current position (forward/backward)
   - `hexi::buffer_seek::end` - seek from end

3. **`update_header_at_position`**: 
   - First writes a placeholder header (4 bytes for `uint32_t`)
   - Writes some body data
   - Seeks back to position 0 using `buffer_seek::beg`
   - Overwrites the placeholder with the actual header value
   - Seeks to the end to restore normal write position

